[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673124742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123506#issuecomment-5673124742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123506","id":5673124742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUiUDhg","user":{"login":"jejay","id":4773902,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzM5MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4773902?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay","html_url":"https://github.com/jejay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:09:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T03:31:13Z","body":"But this removes specular from omni lights (and I think spot lights, untested)\r\n\r\n## Vanilla\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"specular-sphere-vanilla\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5cfe3276-d9f0-4d6a-a865-ee3f8525956b\" />\r\n\r\n## This PR\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"specular-sphere-clayjohn\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c7eb5a8-eaa7-4599-b76e-fb7bed91b82e\" />\r\n\r\n## My PR\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"specular-sphere-myfix\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33779fa4-8c91-4913-a6ea-22c330eb0f37\" />\r\n\r\nThree screenshots, fresh from my TV\r\n\r\n> It's 0/~~2~~1 so far on a trivial code change. And if this code every becomes correct it will only be because an ~~expert~~AI held your hand through the process.\r\n\r\nTo twist your own words against you... AI saw this immediately. I do not understand the refusal to use modern technologies. But thanks for trying, it might even be the right direction, I do not dispute that.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673124742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673438240","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123506#issuecomment-5673438240","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123506","id":5673438240,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUinMIA","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T01:48:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T03:31:19Z","body":"> But this removes specular from omni lights (and I think spot lights, untested)\r\n\r\nThanks for testing! Indeed, the changed code was only in the `USE_LIGHT_DIRECTIONAL` branch. We need to ensure that specular light gets added even when there are no directional lights in the scene. Added a fix already.\r\n\r\n> To twist your own words against you... AI saw this immediately. I do not understand the refusal to use modern technologies. But thanks for trying, it might even be the right direction, I do not dispute that.\r\n\r\nThis really isn't the dunk you think it is. You caught an obvious error in a PR I made in 30 minutes touching code I haven't looked at in 5 years. \r\n\r\nYour PRs were rejected not because they used AI, but because they were totally wrong. Its fine to use AI to help you. But don't try to force bad code on the project. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673438240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673689475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123506#issuecomment-5673689475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123506","id":5673689475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUi2hgw","user":{"login":"jejay","id":4773902,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzM5MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4773902?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay","html_url":"https://github.com/jejay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jejay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T02:21:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T03:07:24Z","body":"I'm happy with it getting improved, I genuinley agree that this might be a better fix now, not that my opinnion is too important here. I did never force my PR onto the project.\r\n\r\nBut this fix still changes more than just the bug I was describing:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"platformer-omni-vanilla\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b25c63ad-9fe0-49a9-a309-8c0b600f037f\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"platformer-omni-clayjohn\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/92ca5351-f1a4-4f83-a0cf-1cb87e744656\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"300\" alt=\"platformer-omni-one-myfix\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd3c5a03-7202-4655-ae7a-c6565eff3d65\" />\r\n\r\nThe order is again, vanilla, your fix, my fix. As you can see, your fix changes how the scene looks. Maybe this new look is actually an improvement, then yes, you fixed a second bug. (Btw vanilla has the environment reflections because this is a slightly altered project, the robot is in omni light, no shadow)\r\n\r\nBut that bug was already in there. You sent me the wrong way by claiming I introduced this bug. As it stands my PRs are the only ones that do not change any visuals except the one that both our PRs claim to care are about.\r\n\r\n> You caught an obvious error in a PR I made in 30 minutes touching code I haven't looked at in 5 years.\r\n\r\nWasn't that what I said? That it is likely even for the maintainers hard to grasp their own ancient code? Almost everything in your reviews of my PRs was wrong, this fix cannot be a one liner, I did not introduce the scatter code on top of direct light. My PRs did not introduce new regressions. Yet you scuffed me and then introduced the only of the three PRs with a regression. An obvious one, as you call it.\r\n\r\nAll that really holds is that my PRs did not fix the other bug, the scatter/direct light bug. That's true, and a reason to go with yours. But we could have worked together on this if you weren't so hostile, even your wrong feedback was valuable such that my AI could find the other bug, and I then explained it to you. Maybe we would have gotten there together.\r\n\r\nAnd nothing would have happened if I would not have found and pushed this after these two bugs being in there for five years.\r\n\r\nEdit: I cross checked this with the normal fragment lighting version and yes, yours indeed looks closer to it. Might be still a breaking change in the sense that people were relying on the wrong behaviour. You are hiding a much bigger fix behind that title. In contrast, it is less likely that someone is relying on the environment reflections being removed in shadows, so it is easier to argue for shipping mine as a fix version. I do not want to force my PR, though. I just want to reiterate, that my PRs were not as bad as you made them out to be.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5673689475/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5675471459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123506#issuecomment-5675471459","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123506","id":5675471459,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUkjSYw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":